              "type": "context",
              "content": "Your status line script runs frequently during active sessions. Commands like `git status` or `git diff` can be slow, especially in large repositories. This example caches git information to a temp file and only refreshes it every 5 seconds."
            },
            {
              "type": "context",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "removed",
              "content": "Use a stable, fixed filename for the cache file like `/tmp/statusline-git-cache`. Each status line invocation runs as a new process, so process-based identifiers like `$$`, `os.getpid()`, or `process.pid` produce a different value every time and the cache is never reused."
            },
            {
              "type": "added",
              "content": "The cache filename needs to be stable across status line invocations within a session, but unique across sessions so concurrent sessions in different repositories don't read each other's cached git state. Process-based identifiers like `$$`, `os.getpid()`, or `process.pid` change on every invocation and defeat the cache. Use the `session_id` from the JSON input instead: it's stable for the lifetime of a session and unique per session."
            },
